WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.772
A diagram needs a question and a legend.

00:00:02.772 --> 00:00:09.703
Boxes may represent domain concepts, modules,
processes, or machines; arrows may mean very
different

00:00:09.703 --> 00:00:10.188
things.

00:00:10.188 --> 00:00:16.841
The four plus one model separates logical, process,
development, and physical concerns, and uses

00:00:16.841 --> 00:00:18.643
scenarios to connect them.

00:00:18.643 --> 00:00:21.623
Choose a view for the question being asked.

00:00:21.623 --> 00:00:28.415
Then check that the views agree about the same
system, without trying to put every detail into one

00:00:28.415 --> 00:00:29.524
crowded picture.

00:00:29.524 --> 00:00:35.575
Reusable architectural ideas include styles,
reference architectures, and product-line

00:00:35.575 --> 00:00:36.560
architectures.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:41.134
Their assumptions and constraints matter as much as
their shapes.

00:00:41.134 --> 00:00:46.270
C4 offers nested descriptions: context, containers,
components, and code.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:49.507
These levels help match detail to an audience.

00:00:49.507 --> 00:00:56.473
A container here means a running application or data
store, not necessarily a packaging technology.

00:00:56.473 --> 00:01:03.087
C4 levels and four plus one views are complementary
ways to organize descriptions, rather than

00:01:03.087 --> 00:01:04.635
interchangeable lists.

00:01:04.635 --> 00:01:08.916
Patterns organize responsibilities around recurring
problems.

00:01:08.916 --> 00:01:15.371
Three-tier architecture separates presentation,
application processing, and data management.

00:01:15.371 --> 00:01:22.388
MVC focuses on model, view, and controller
responsibilities, while sense, compute, control
organizes

00:01:22.388 --> 00:01:24.002
observation and action.

00:01:24.002 --> 00:01:29.897
These are useful ideas, but labels do not establish
deployment or guarantee quality.

00:01:29.897 --> 00:01:34.107
Explain the problem, the relationships, and the
constraints.

00:01:34.107 --> 00:01:40.913
Then examine whether the proposed arrangement serves
the system mission and stakeholder concerns.
